Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:41:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] licensing: send compact JWE delegation tickets to the
 licensing service as t=.

The licensing service, like Xbox, rejects a compact JWE delegation ticket in the d= form: the
licenses/content request then fails with HTTP 401, after sign-in and the package lookup succeed.
The conversion Xbox's user authentication uses moves to models::secrets, and the device's and the
user's tickets for the licensing service go through it too. Opaque tickets keep d=.

Reported in https://github.com/xodus-gaming/xodus/issues/238: with both tickets as t=, the
content license request succeeds.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: xbox-ticket
